{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgF8q1P7jPSPgMucnUYqm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"prompt\": \"A square abstract painting that fills the entire image edge to edge, with no frame, border, wall, room, or gallery setting. Purely nonrepresentational: no recognizable objects, figures, faces, bodies, scenes, landscapes, horizons, machines, diagrams, symbols, icons, letters, numbers, or text. The palette is dominated by deep indigo and cold slate grey, with a single restless vein of hot vermilion and ochre running diagonally across the lower third, and small islands of pale bone white near the upper edge. Composition: a dense, heavily layered lower-left mass built from many scraped, overpainted strata, which thins into open, untouched cream-colored space toward the upper right. The brushwork alternates between rapid, tight dry-brush hatching and broad, sweeping palette-knife gestures that drag color past their own edges. Texture is thick and uneven, with ridges of impasto catching light, and some areas are sanded back so the underlayers show through. Rhythm comes from repeated short strokes that accelerate in one band and then suddenly stop, leaving raw gaps. Spatial tension: the vermilion line pushes against the cold mass as if trying to break through it, and a few strokes hover at the boundary between the dense area and the empty space, unresolved. The overall feeling is of pressure held against restraint, urgency checked by care, with the emptiness on the right left deliberately open and unfinished.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":570,"cache_read_input_tokens":17673,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":570},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"con